24560111|t|Hepatocellular carcinoma: diagnosis, management, and prognosis.
24560111|a|The successful management of hepatocellular carcinoma (HCC) requires a multidisciplinary approach, incorporating hepatologists, oncologists, surgical oncologists, transplant surgeons, and radiologists. With improvements in technology and better long-term outcomes data, management strategies for HCC have become more methodical and more successful. This article focuses on some of the most critical advances relating to carcinogenesis, surveillance, and management. 
